# Kmeet Environment Configuration

# ========================================
# TURN Server Configuration (Coturn)
# ========================================
# Your custom TURN server URL (e.g., your EC2 instance)
# Format: turn:your-domain.com:3478 OR turn:your-ip-address:3478
TURN_SERVER_URL=turn:43.205.187.5:3478

# TURN server username (configured in your Coturn server)
TURN_USERNAME=your-turn-username

# TURN server password/credential (configured in your Coturn server)
TURN_PASSWORD=your-turn-password

# ========================================
# Server Configuration
# ========================================
# Session Secret - A secure random string used to sign session cookies
# REQUIRED: Generate a secure random string for production
# Example: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=your-secret-key-here

# PORT is automatically set by Replit, do not modify
# PORT=5000

# Node Environment
# Automatically set to 'development' by npm run dev
# NODE_ENV=development

# ========================================
# Additional Notes
# ========================================
# 1. To use your Coturn TURN server:
#    - Set TURN_SERVER_URL to your EC2 public IP or domain
#    - Set TURN_USERNAME and TURN_PASSWORD to match your Coturn configuration
#    - The app will automatically use these credentials via /api/turn-credentials endpoint
#
# 2. To test TURN server connectivity:
#    - Check Coturn logs: sudo journalctl -u coturn -f
#    - Verify port 3478 (UDP/TCP) and 5349 (TLS) are open in security group
#    - Test with: https://webrtc.github.io/samples/src/content/peerconnection/trickle-ice/
#
# 3. If TURN server is not configured:
#    - App will fall back to public STUN servers
#    - P2P connections may fail across different networks (NAT/firewall)

